score_etherfi.json is a regenerated score document (see routers/company.py's payload
shape). Write it back MINIFIED and on ONE line — `json.dumps(doc, separators=(",", ":"))`,
no trailing newline. Pretty-printing it turns a 20-line regeneration into a 41,000-line diff.

score_etherfi.json remains the legacy 1.4.1 document for backward-compatible
reader regressions; the original analysis inputs are unavailable here.
score_current_synthetic.json is generated through the current fold with explicit
synthetic inputs (not an Etherfi replay). It preserves an upgrade finding with
$2M observed holdings with a numeric security score/confidence and separately unknown dollar exposure.
Its holdings amount is scoped to observed own holdings, with incomplete coverage
and freshness explicitly recorded; it is not a claim about future assets.
Regenerate using: .venv/bin/python -m tests.regenerate_current_score_fixture
